==English==
{{wp|Motte (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology===
* As a {{der|en|fr|-}}, {{der|en|wa|-}}, and {{der|en|vls|-}} surname, from {{der|en|fro|mot|mot, motte|t=embankment, hill, mound}}, from {{der|en|ML.|mota|t=fortified height}}, which could be of {{der|en|cel|-}} origin and from {{der|en|cel-gau|*mutt}}, {{m|cel-gau|*mutta}} (compare {{cog|cy|mwd|t=vault,  arch, canopy}}, {{cog|ga|móta|t=moat}}, though this itself could have been borrowed from the English) or otherwise of {{der|en|gem|-}} origin and from the root of {{m|en|mud}}. Compare {{m|en|Delamotte}}, {{m|en|Demotte}}, {{m|en|Lamotte}}.
* As an English surname, variant of {{m|en|Mott}}.
* As a {{der|en|de|-}} surname, perhaps from {{w|Motten}} in Bavaria, first attested 837, from the personal name {{m|goh|Moto}} (compare {{m|gmw-pro|*mōd|t=courage, bravery}}).

